Upstream snapshot
-----------------
The following directories and files are derived from the upstream
project, redistributed without modification:

  server/                        (entire tree, includes eval_utils, groot,
                                  scripts, docs, debug_image,
                                  socket_test_optimized_AR.py,
                                  test_client_AR.py)
  pyproject.toml                 (top-level)
  LICENSE                        (Apache-2.0 text)
  COPYRIGHT                      (NVIDIA copyright notice)

Snapshot taken at upstream commit:
  ab790c1 ("Update architecture differences in WAN22_BACKBONE.md")

To diff against the original upstream, clone
  https://github.com/dreamzero0/dreamzero.git
and compare to server/.

New contributions in this repository
------------------------------------
The following files are new, authored for this RunPod deployment, and
released under the same Apache-2.0 license:

  README.md
  NOTICE                         (this file)
  client/                        (entire tree)
    README.md
    deoxys_client.py
    robot_client_template.py
    deoxys_configs/dreamzero-joint-impedance.yml
    eval_utils/                  (subset copy of upstream server/eval_utils,
                                  retained for client convenience; same
                                  license as upstream)
  deployment/
    activate.sh
    setup_runpod.sh
    start_server.sh
  docs/
    01_deployment_runpod.md
    02_protocol_reference.md
    03_research_findings.md
    04_client_integration.md
  runs/                          (sample server log + MP4 outputs from a
                                  successful inference session)
  .gitignore

The new contributions reference, but do not redistribute, the following
external dependencies:

  - GEAR-Dreams/DreamZero-DROID model checkpoint (Hugging Face,
    cc-by-nc-4.0; downloaded at setup time, NOT included in this repo)
  - Wan-AI/Wan2.1-I2V-14B-480P backbone (Hugging Face;
    auto-downloaded by the inference server on first launch)
  - UT-Austin-RPL/deoxys_control (Apache-2.0; client-side dependency,
    NOT vendored)

Researched but not redistributed
--------------------------------
The DreamZero gripper / action / control conventions documented in
docs/03_research_findings.md were derived in part by reading code from:

  - arhanjain/sim-evals          (Apache-2.0)
  - droid-dataset/droid          (MIT)
  - UT-Austin-RPL/deoxys_control (Apache-2.0)

We cite specific files and line numbers in that document; we do not
redistribute their code here.
